  <div class="post-meta"><span>2025</span><span class="blog-tag">IRS News</span><span>Guzman Tax Accounting</span></div>
  <div class="post-featured-img"><img src="/assets/img-54.webp" alt="Key Tax Changes from the One Big Beautiful Bill Act" loading="lazy"/></div>
  <div class="post-content"><p>The <strong>One Big Beautiful Bill Act (OBBBA)</strong> introduces several important tax changes that directly affect Latino families and businesses in the U.S.</p><h2>1. Extension of Reduced Tax Rates</h2><p>The tax rates introduced by the 2017 Tax Cuts and Jobs Act (TCJA) become <strong>permanent</strong>. They will no longer expire at the end of 2025.</p><h2>2. Expanded SALT Deduction</h2><p>The deduction limit rises from <strong>$10,000 to $40,000</strong> between 2025 and 2029 (or $20,000 for those filing separately), with a gradual phase-out for incomes above $500,000.</p><h2>3. Benefits for Families</h2><p>Several tax credits for families with children are expanded, and the income limits to qualify for the Child Tax Credit are adjusted.</p><h2>How Does This Affect You?</h2><p>These changes could mean significant savings on your taxes. Schedule a consultation with us to find out exactly how your specific situation benefits.</p><a href="/en/consultation" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top:8px;">Schedule Consultation</a></div>
